# netsurf: a settings page (patch 241; roadmap WS-E, Phase 1 exit)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 240)
#
# The Phase 1 bar asks for a settings page (user agent, zoom, blocking);
# the only way to change any of them was to edit files on the card.
#
#  - vita/remote.c: the browser's own listener serves /settings, and
#    /settings?KEY=VALUE applies one setting, saves it, and shows the page
#    again with "Saved: ...". Only to this device: accept() records the
#    peer, and anything but 127.0.0.1 (or the device's own address, for a
#    stack that reports loopback that way) gets 403 -- the LAN may open
#    pages on the Vita, not change its settings.
#  - vita/chrome.c: the page (current choice highlighted, the others as
#    links); vita_chrome_set(): ua = a preset (chrome / safari / firefox /
#    vita: written to useragent.txt and applied at once), zoom = a zoom
#    step (applied to the window now, and where new windows start),
#    blocking = on / off. zoom and blocking are kept in
#    ux0:data/VitaBrowser/settings.txt, read at start-up. The home page's
#    controls line links "Settings".
#  - vita/resolve.c: vita_resolve_blocking turns the block list off.
#  - vita/interact.c: C_SETTING (in effect, saved, and for the user agent
#    what sites are sent) and seven steps: open the page, firefox,
#    blocking off, zoom 125%, then back to chrome / on / 100%. Placed
#    before IN-download so the history check still sees that page last.
#
